# What must never go into a Docker build context.
#
# The context is this whole folder, and it is uploaded to the Docker daemon on
# every build. Without this file that means sending caddy.exe (~49 MB), the
# live database, and — the one that actually matters — .env and Web.txt, both
# of which contain real secrets. The Dockerfile only COPYs app/, so none of it
# would end up in the image, but there is no reason to hand it to the daemon at
# all, and on a 1 GB ARM NAS the wasted transfer is not free either.

.env
*.env
!.env.example
Web.txt

relay.db
relay.db-journal
relay.db-wal
relay.db-shm
test_*.db

caddy.exe
caddy_data/
caddy_config/

.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
venv/
.venv/

# The nested Qt helper project and the public mirror — neither belongs in an
# image of the Python relay.
MediaCountdownsRelay/
Media Countdowns Relay Server Public/

*.bat
*.lnk
query.txt
